v0.8.3 - June 2026

symlinks
 * first-class support for symlinks in fstree and related subsystems

ipc
 * replace client/server pulse with ping / pong messages, more robust to peer timeout
 * refactor into channel / pipe / ring which handle timeouts correctly
 * adds per-pipe performance counters
 * rcu rewrite for robustness, metrics

identity
 * adopts a standardized identity construction across vertex types
 * uses bech32 encoded 12 byte truncated sha1 hash over canonical string

namespaces
 * new namespace system which replaces the fsindex
 * used in module imports, bind rules, formula refs, lookup selector, plugin file / args / envs
 * namespace resolutions take refs and invalidations propagate upwards via these refs

disintegrate
 * consolidated logic around vertex and edges cleanup into disintegrate operation
 * improved visiblity and robustness
 * centralized place for synchronization

build
 * build records which persist build metadata, available via //bm/build-records
 * formula records which persist individual execution metadata, available via //bm/formula-records
 * configurable retention for these records
 * new build slot vars and build events

client
 * bam build is now the default command
 * robust disambiguation of command names from file paths, moved to the lexer
 * other args parsing improvements
 * various new commands
 * bam rma run command, run rma on demand and trace its execution
 * bam blame command, show details of most recent exec that updated a node

plugins
 * detail nodes that expose trailing stdin, stdout, stderr, auxout, of the plugin process
 * sysvars rendered to plugins env, like formulas

modules
 * removed the require keyword
 * adds mak as an alternative text format for varfiles, filename var.mak
 * managed keyword, to enable management of the module build dir. when this setting is active
   non-primary files are actively unlinked from the build dir - it only contains artifacts.

fstrees
 * new unlink setting to control whether bam will perform unlink operations on paths in that fstree.
   active pruning of managed module dirs requires unlink and mkdir be enabled.
 * readlink changed from boolean to trinary of yes, no, required. if required and readlink fails,
   reconciliation will also fail.

bacon
 * support for application defined bacon value types
 * various parser improvements
 * package and export the perl bacon bindings

v0.8.2 - September 2024

New plugins system, and the first two plugins. See the builtin-plugins directory.

Most requests now return a bacon-valued result. In most cases you now need to parse the bacon text.

The special-purpose describe commands have been removed. Instead, there are named nodes in the
shadow fs that represent different aspects of the runtime state. This state can be retrieved with
the describe command on these nodes, whose result is bacon text, or in some cases, the tell command,
whose result is a binary blob that has a descriptor in libbam.

The format of describe results across object types have been standardized, and relationships between
objects are now included in these results. Every object is addressable by its id, so this provides a
nice mechanism to iteratively browse through the graph.

New naming for special files, configset, varset, ruleset

filesystem
 * config sections filesystems and walker have been replaced by the filesystem section and the
   fstrees subsection

v0.8.1 - February 2024

mass rename across the project from fab -> bam

build
 * added a configure/make based build for package distribution
 * there is now a distribution of bam on the aur which uses this

tests
 * the integ tests now use the user run dir instead of the system run dir

bam
 * new buildplan command
 * bam will now kill any competing bamd processes before starting bamd
 * moved the ipc dir to users run directory

bamd
 * bamd will no longer run indefinitely. the timeout is configurable.

v0.8.0 - December 2023

config
 * config.bam files in the ancestry of the module are now applied
 * config is now strictly cumulative

vars
 * var.bam files in the ancestry of the module are now applied
 * vars are now strictly cumulative

rules
 * rules.bam files in the ancestry of the module are now applied
 * new bind rule type
 * new search/search rule type
 * conditional blocks are now supported, expressions resolve against the module vars

anchor
 * a module may now specify an anchor directory -- rules are also run in the anchor dir by default.
   in this way, out-of-tree builds are now well supported.

patterns
 * type qualifiers have been added, e.g. foo(/) to limit matches to directories named foo

filesystem
 * mkdirs config option, if enabled, will cause fabd to create missing directories
 * indexed config option, controls whether dirents are indexed for lookup by name

fab client
 * new commands: envs, filesystem, fstree, rules
 * stats -S: show stats from special files only
 * config: now shows file and location next to each value

fab commander has been removed

v0.7.0 - July 2021

formula features
 * new rule types zero x many (useful for generated files)
 * path-search (search path specified in config)

new builtin modules
 * git

fab client features
 * event subscription
 * new commands stats, tree, ls, several others
 * configuration file

fab commander features
 * shows node stats
 * switch between filesystem and dependency graph explorers

reconciliation system for applying changes live
 * module files
 * formula files
 * var files
 * config files

other
 * fabd now supports multiple concurrent clients
 * integration test suite added

v0.6.0 - May 2020

The v0.6 release represents a rewrite of most of the functionality of the
project. It is NOT backwards compatible with the v0.5 series. To upgrade, you
will have to replace fabfiles with module.bam files which have an entirely
different syntax.

v0.5.4.0 - July 2018

The v0.5 branch is used to build the master branch. This release is aimed at
making it easier to set up a new environment for building the master branch. In
particular the fab build logic should not rely on modules provided by the
previous version.

* clean up some compile time errors and warnings to permit building with newer
  compilers
* add an option to allow specifying directories for resolving invocations with
  higher precedence than the builtin directories provided by fab

